Template: strata/mirror-disks
Type: multiselect
Choices-C: ${DEVS}
Choices: ${CHOICES}
Description: The two system disks (mirror)
 StrataOS is installed on both disks at once (RAID 1): the NAS keeps
 starting and running when one of them fails.
 .
 Choose exactly two disks, ideally of the same size. Both are completely
 erased. Data disks are added later from the web interface: do not select
 them here.

Template: strata/mirror-wrong
Type: error
Description: Choose two disks
 The system mirror needs exactly two disks.

Template: strata/datadisks-disks
Type: multiselect
Choices-C: ${DEVS}
Choices: ${CHOICES}
Description: The data disks (the system goes on each of them)
 StrataOS takes about 22 GB at the start of each chosen disk: a copy of the
 system on each (RAID 1), so the NAS keeps starting while one disk is left.
 The rest of each disk becomes a data partition, where you create your
 volumes from the web interface.
 .
 Choose two disks or more (eight at most). They are completely erased.

Template: strata/datadisks-wrong
Type: error
Description: Choose two disks or more
 The system on the data disks needs two to eight disks.
